{% doc %}
  Authorization gate for the module's single generic ActionCable channel,
  `pos_websocket`. Must echo the literal string 'true' or 'false' — this is
  platformOS's native WebSocket convention (see
  https://documentation.platformos.com/use-cases/using-websockets), not
  something this module invents.

  Private by default. A room only becomes joinable once something has
  called commands/rooms/find_or_create for it — until then nobody can join,
  including its would-be creator's own next request racing against
  itself. Once registered:
    - public rooms  (public: true)  — any logged-in user may join
    - private rooms (public: false) — only registered members (the creator,
      added automatically, plus anyone added via commands/rooms/members/add)
  See modules/websocket/lib/queries/rooms/authorized.liquid for the actual
  check (shared with receive.liquid so the two can't drift apart).

  Apps needing a different policy entirely should override this file — copy
  it to app/modules/websocket/public/views/partials/channels/pos_websocket/subscribed.liquid
  per the Module Override System.
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  assign room_id = context.params.room_id

  if context.current_user == blank
    echo 'false'
  else
    function authorized = 'modules/websocket/queries/rooms/authorized', room_id: room_id, user_id: context.current_user.id

    if authorized
      echo 'true'
    else
      echo 'false'
    endif
  endif
%}
